      "Answer: Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has two main components: (i) a retrieval mechanism that retrieves relevant documents or information from an external knowledge source, and (ii) a generation module that processes this information to generate human-like text [1].  The retrieval mechanism finds relevant information, while the generation module uses that information to create the final output [1, 2].  Different approaches exist for integrating these components, such as input-layer, output-layer, and intermediate-layer integration [2].  Furthermore, the granularity of retrieved data and the type of data source are important factors [3].\n",
